bles.user_id\").\n\n6. **Stage 6 (100% Diagnostic Step Recall Mandate)**: You MUST extract EVERY SINGLE step described in the procedure section of the raw SOP text. Omitting any diagnostic or verification step is STRICTLY PROHIBITED.\n\n7. **Stage 7 (Conditional Branch Mapping & execute_if)**: If the raw SOP specifies conditional skip instructions, map this logic into valid `execute_if` boolean expressions (e.g., `execute_if: variables.account_found == 'true'`).\n\n8. **Stage 8 (Dynamic Timeout Allocation by Action Scope)**: Assign `timeout_seconds` dynamically: Quick Info Read / API Call (30s), System Scan / Diagnostic Audit (90s), Full Repair / Heavy Job (300s).\n\n9. **CRITICAL MANDATE (Omit GUI Window Setup Steps)**: DO NOT generate non-executable GUI setup steps like \"Open Command Prompt\" or \"Open Web Browser\". Start directly with functional actions.\n\n10. **CRITICAL MANDATE (Zero Unwritten Action Addition)**: You are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from inventing or adding steps/tool calls (such as `send_email` or `search_users`) that are NOT explicitly stated in the raw SOP document.\n\n11. **CRITICAL MANDATE (Omit Manual Human/Verbal Confirmation Steps)**: Human/verbal/ticket confirmation checks, manual admin approvals, and user clarification steps are currently PAUSED. Omit non-automated verbal/ticket confirmation steps and start directly with automated API tool calls (`tool_call`) and CLI system commands (`command`).\n\n\n## OUTPUT JSON SCHEMA MANDATE\nCRITICAL FORMATTING MANDATE:\n- All keys and string values MUST be enclosed in standard DOUBLE QUOTES (\").\n- NEVER use Python single quotes (') for dictionary keys or strings.\n- Return raw, valid JSON only matching this schema:\n```json\n{\n    \"reasoning_chain\": [\n        \"[Stage 1 Verification Gates]: Gate 1 (Function match) -> Gate 2 (Provider active) -> Gate 3 (Problem aligned) -> Gate 4 (Params complete) -> Result: tool_call | command\",\n        \"[Stage 2 Sequencing]: Ordered search/diagnostic steps before remediation\",\n        \"[Stage 3 Variables]: Formatted {{entities.var}} placeholders\",\n        \"[Stage 4 Fallbacks]: Mapped fallback actions\",\n        \"[Stage 5 Verification]: Added output parse instructions\",\n        \"[Stage 6 Recall]: Preserved 100% of diagnostic steps\",\n        \"[Stage 7 Branching]: Mapped execute_if conditions\",\n        \"[Stage 8 Timeouts]: Assigned timeout_seconds\"\n    ],\n    \"sop_id\": \"SOP-{file_name_slug}-001\",\n    \"title\": \"Title of Playbook\",\n    \"category\": \"network | storage | system | logins | software | hardware\",\n    \"target_os\": \"windows | linux\",\n    \"description\": \"Comprehensive overview of what this playbook does\",\n    \"required_entities\": [\"user_id\", \"email\", \"hostname\"],\n    \"trigger_words\": [\"unlock\", \"account\", \"login\"],\n    \"steps\": [\n        {\n            \"step_number\": 1,\n            \"sop_step_description\": \"Detailed step objective\",\n            \"step_type\": \"tool_call | command\",\n            \"platform\": \"high-level vendor/platform inferred from SOP or tool catalog (only for tool_call, else null)\",\n            \"provider\": \"active_provider_name (from REGISTERED API TOOLS CATALOG above, only for tool_call, else null)\",\n            \"function_name\": \"exact_function_name (from REGISTERED API TOOLS CATALOG above, only for tool_call, else null)\",\n            \"comm_inputs\": {\n                \"user_id\": \"{{entities.user_id}}\"\n            },\n            \"command\": \"ipconfig /all (only for command, else null)\",\n            \"shell\": \"powershell (only for command, else null)\",\n            \"fallback_command\": null,\n            \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n            \"expected_output_contains\": \"unlocked\",\n            \"timeout_seconds\": 30,\n            \"output_variable\": \"step_result\",\n            \"output_parse_instruction\": \"Inspect output/JSON response and set status flags.\",\n            \"execute_if\": null,\n            \"is_dangerous\": false,\n            \"danger_warning\": null\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n## RAW SOP DOCUMENT TEXT TO TRANSLATE:\nSOP-L1-APP-001\n\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\nSTANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE\n\nSoftware Application Unblock\nRequest\nEndpoint Support  ﬁ  Application Management\n\nSOP ID\n\nSupport Level\n\nCategory\n\nSOP-L1-APP-001\n\nL1 Service Desk\n\nEndpoint Support / Application Management\n\nPrimary Remediation Path\n\nIFEO Debugger Entry Removal\n\nDocument Version\n\n1.0\n\nStatus\n\nClassification\n\nApproved for Use\n\nInternal Use Only\n\nThis document defines the standard, command-based process for identifying an\napplication block caused by an Image File Execution Options (IFEO) debugger entry\nand removing it as a fallback remediation on a Windows endpoint.\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\n\nPage 1\n\n\fSOP-L1-APP-001\n\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\n.  Table of Contents\n\n1.\n\n2.\n\n3.\n\n4.\n\nObjective\n\nPreconditions\n\nProcess Flow Overview\n\nDetailed Procedure\n\nStep 1 — Verify Endpoint Connectivity\n\nStep 2 — Identify Application Blocking Mechanism\n\nStep 3 — Remove IFEO Block (Fallback)\n\nStep 4 — Refresh Local Policy\n\nStep 5 — Verify Block Removal\n\nStep 6 — Validate Resolution\n\nStep 7 — Update Ticket\n\n5.\n\n6.\n\nEscalation Criteria\n\nDocument Control\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\n\nPage 2\n\n\fSOP-L1-APP-001\n\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\n1.  Objective\n\nRestore access to an approved software application that is blocked on a Windows endpoint by identifying the\nblocking mechanism and applying the appropriate remediation. If the block is caused by an Image File\nExecution Options (IFEO) debugger entry, remove the entry as a fallback remediation.\n\n2.  Preconditions\n\nTicket assigned to L1 Engineer.\n\n(cid:127) Remote administrative access to the endpoint.\n\n(cid:127) User device is online.\n\nAdministrative privileges available.\n\n3.  Process Flow Overview\n\nThe diagram below summarizes the end-to-end decision flow. Full instructions for each stage are provided in\nSection 4, Detailed Procedure.\n\n1. Verify\nConnectivity\n\n2. Identify Blocking\nMechanism\n\n3–5. Remove, Refresh\n& Verify\n\nIs the application blocked via an IFEO Debugger entry? (Step 2)\n\nYES — IFEO Debugger Entry Found\n\nNO — Registry Key Not Found\n\nProceed to Step 3 — remove the Debugger entry\n(and the key itself if it exists solely to block the app),\nthen refresh policy and verify.\n\nApplication is not blocked through IFEO. Investigate\nAppLocker, WDAC, Intune, or Endpoint Security\npolicies, or escalate to L2.\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\n\nPage 3\n\n(cid:127)\n(cid:127)\nﬁ\nﬁ\n\fSOP-L1-APP-001\n\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\n4.  Detailed Procedure\n\nSTEP 1  —  Verify Endpoint Connectivity\n\nCommand\n\nTest-Connection <ComputerName> -Count 2\n\n4 Expected Result: Reply received from target system.\n\nIf unreachable — Action:\n\nVerify VPN / network connectivity.\n\n(cid:127) Retry.\n\nEscalate if unreachable.\n\nSTEP 2  —  Identify Application Blocking Mechanism\n\nCommand\n\nreg query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\"\n\nExpected Result 1\n\nDebugger    REG_SZ    ...\n\nResult: Application is blocked using IFEO. Proceed to Step 3.\n\nExpected Result 2\n\nERROR:\nThe system was unable to find the specified registry key.\n\nResult: Application is not blocked through IFEO. Investigate other blocking technologies (AppLocker, WDAC,\nIntune, Endpoint Security) or escalate to L2.\n\nSTEP 3  —  Remove IFEO Block (Fallback)\n\nExecute only when Step 2 confirms an IFEO Debugger entry.\n\nRemove Debugger Value\n\nreg delete \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\" ^\n  /v Debugger /f\n\nIf the application-specific IFEO key was created only for blocking, remove the key:\n\nreg delete \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\" ^\n  /f\n\nSTEP 4  —  Refresh Local Policy\n\nCommand\n\ngpupdate /force\n\n4 Expected Result: Computer Policy update has completed successfully. User Policy update has completed\nsuccessfully.\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\n\nPage 4\n\n(cid:127)\n(cid:127)\n\fSOP-L1-APP-001\n\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\nSTEP 5  —  Verify Block Removal\n\nCommand\n\nreg query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\"\n\n4 Expected Result: ERROR: The system was unable to find the specified registry key — or — Debugger\nvalue not present.\n\nSTEP 6  —  Validate Resolution\n\nAsk the user to launch the application.\n\n4 Expected Result:\n\nApplication launches successfully.\n\n(cid:127) No error message displayed.\n\n(cid:127) User confirms issue resolved.\n\nIf the application remains blocked:\n\n(cid:127) Check for AppLocker policies.\n\n(cid:127) Check WDAC policies.\n\n(cid:127) Check Endpoint Security policies.\n\nEscalate to L2 Support.\n\nSTEP 7  —  Update Ticket\n\nResolution Notes\n\nIssue:\nApplication launch blocked.\n\nRoot Cause:\nIFEO Debugger registry entry prevented application execution.\n\nAction Taken:\nVerified IFEO configuration.\nRemoved Debugger registry entry.\nRefreshed Group Policy.\nValidated successful application launch.\n\nStatus:\nResolved.\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\n\nPage 5\n\n(cid:127)\n(cid:127)\n\fSOP-L1-APP-001\n\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\n5.  Escalation Criteria\n\nEscalate to L2 if:\n\nIFEO key not present.\n\nApplication blocked by WDAC.\n\nApplication blocked by AppLocker.\n\nEndpoint protection policy prevents execution.\n\n(cid:127) Registry modification fails.\n\n(cid:127) User lacks required permissions.\n\nApplication still fails after remediation.\n\n6.  Document Control\n\nAttribute\n\nSOP ID\n\nTitle\n\nCategory\n\nValue\n\nSOP-L1-APP-001\n\nSoftware Application Unblock Request\n\nEndpoint Support ﬁ Application Management\n\nSupport Level\n\nL1 Service Desk\n\nPrimary Remediation Path\n\nIFEO Debugger Entry Removal\n\nVersion\n\nStatus\n\n1.0\n\nApproved for use\n\nIT Service Desk — Confidential / Internal Use Only\n\nPage 6\n\n(cid:127)\n(cid:127)\n(cid:127)\n(cid:127)\n(cid:127)\n\n\nAI: [{'name': 'list_available_platforms', 'args': {}, 'id': 'reNqCwUVG', 'type': 'tool_call'}]\nTool: [\n  {\n    \"platform\": \"mock\",\n    \"provider\": \"l1_testing_platform_api\",\n    \"description\": \"L1 Support Platform REST API client \\u2014 covers user auth, password reset/change, MFA reset/enable/verify, account lock/unlock, user search, and audit logs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"platform\": \"auth0\",\n    \"provider\": \"auth0_user_management\",\n    \"description\": \"Auth0 User Identity Management tools for searching users, triggering password reset emails, and unlocking accounts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"platform\": \"email\",\n    \"provider\": \"email_service\",\n    \"description\": \"Email and communication service for sending ticket updates, resolution tokens, and notifications to users.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"platform\": \"airretailer\",\n    \"provider\": \"airretailer_vpn_rdp_tools\",\n    \"description\": \"AirRetailer VPN and Remote Desktop (RDP) tools \\u2014 VPN portal login, Cisco AnyConnect client installer/settings, VPN connection, and RDP session setup.\"\n  }\n]"
  ]
