ly removed.\n  - `{{variables.application_launches}}`: Set to `true` if user confirms application launch.\n\n---\n\n#### **Stage 4 (Strict SOP Command Fidelity & Zero Unwritten Action Hallucinations)**\n- **Explicitly written actions** in the SOP:\n  1. `Test-Connection <ComputerName> -Count 2`\n  2. `reg query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\"`\n  3. `reg delete \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\" /v Debugger /f`\n  4. `reg delete \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\" /f`\n  5. `gpupdate /force`\n  6. `reg query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Image File Execution Options\\<Application>.exe\"`\n- **No unwritten actions** (e.g., `send_email`, `search_users`) are added.\n\n---\n\n#### **Stage 5 (Verification & Output Parsing Instructions)**\n- **Command steps** require output parsing:\n  1. **Step 1 (Connectivity)**: Check for `Reply from <ComputerName>`.\n  2. **Step 2 (Identify Block)**: Check for `Debugger REG_SZ` (set `ifeo_block_confirmed = true`) or `ERROR` (set `ifeo_block_confirmed = false`).\n  3. **Step 3 (Remove Block)**: Check for `The operation completed successfully`.\n  4. **Step 5 (Verify Removal)**: Check for `ERROR` (set `ifeo_removed = true`).\n  5. **Step 6 (Validate Resolution)**: User confirmation (omitted per mandate).\n\n---\n\n#### **Stage 6 (100% Diagnostic Step Recall Mandate)**\n- **All steps** in the SOP are preserved:\n  1. Verify connectivity.\n  2. Identify blocking mechanism.\n  3. Remove IFEO block.\n  4. Refresh local policy.\n  5. Verify block removal.\n  6. Validate resolution (omitted per mandate).\n\n---\n\n#### **Stage 7 (Conditional Branch Mapping & execute_if)**\n- **Conditional logic**:\n  - **Step 3 (Remove IFEO Block)**: Execute only if `{{variables.ifeo_block_confirmed}} == 'true'`.\n  - **Step 4 (Refresh Policy)**: Execute only if `{{variables.ifeo_removed}} == 'true'`.\n  - **Step 5 (Verify Removal)**: Execute only if `{{variables.ifeo_removed}} == 'true'`.\n\n---\n\n#### **Stage 8 (Dynamic Timeout Allocation by Action Scope)**\n- **Timeout assignments**:\n  1. **Step 1 (Connectivity)**: 30s (quick network check).\n  2. **Step 2 (Identify Block)**: 30s (registry query).\n  3. **Step 3 (Remove Block)**: 30s (registry deletion).\n  4. **Step 4 (Refresh Policy)**: 90s (Group Policy update).\n  5. **Step 5 (Verify Removal)**: 30s (registry query).\n\n---\n\n### Final OKF Playbook JSON Schema\n```json\n{\n    \"reasoning_chain\": [\n        \"[Stage 1 Verification Gates]: Gate 1 (Function match) -> Gate 2 (Provider active) -> Gate 3 (Problem aligned) -> Gate 4 (Params complete) -> Result: command\",\n        \"[Stage 2 Sequencing]: Ordered search/diagnostic steps before remediation\",\n        \"[Stage 3 Variables]: Formatted {{entities.var}} placeholders for computer_name and application_exe\",\n        \"[Stage 4 Fallbacks]: Mapped fallback actions to null (no unwritten steps added)\",\n        \"[Stage 5 Verification]: Added output parse instructions for registry queries and deletions\",\n        \"[Stage 6 Recall]: Preserved 100% of diagnostic steps from the SOP\",\n        \"[Stage 7 Branching]: Mapped execute_if conditions for conditional steps\",\n        \"[Stage 8 Timeouts]: Assigned timeout_seconds based on action scope\"\n    ],\n    \"sop_id\": \"SOP-L1-APP-001\",\n    \"title\": \"Software Application Unblock Request (IFEO Debugger Entry Removal)\",\n    \"category\": \"software\",\n    \"target_os\": \"windows\",\n    \"description\": \"This playbook automates the identification and removal of an Image File Execution Options (IFEO) debugger entry blocking a software application on a Windows endpoint. It includes steps for verifying connectivity, checking for IFEO blocks, removing the block, refreshing local policy, and verifying the remov