  {\n    \"step_number\": 2,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Identify if the application is blocked by an IFEO debugger entry.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"command\",\n    \"platform\": null,\n    \"provider\": null,\n    \"function_name\": null,\n    \"comm_inputs\": null,\n    \"command\": \"reg query \\\"HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Image File Execution Options\\\\{{entities.application_exe}}\\\"\",\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.connectivity_confirmed == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 3,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Remove the IFEO debugger entry for the application.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"command\",\n    \"platform\": null,\n    \"provider\": null,\n    \"function_name\": null,\n    \"comm_inputs\": null,\n    \"command\": \"reg delete \\\"HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Image File Execution Options\\\\{{entities.application_exe}}\\\" /v Debugger /f\",\n    \"fallback_command\": \"reg delete \\\"HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Image File Execution Options\\\\{{entities.application_exe}}\\\" /f\",\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.ifeo_block_confirmed == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 4,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Refresh local Group Policy to apply changes.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"command\",\n    \"platform\": null,\n    \"provider\": null,\n    \"function_name\": null,\n    \"comm_inputs\": null,\n    \"command\": \"gpupdate /force\",\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.ifeo_removed == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 90\n  },\n  {\n    \"step_number\": 5,\n    \"sop_step_description\": \"Verify that the IFEO debugger entry has been removed.\",\n    \"step_type\": \"command\",\n    \"platform\": null,\n    \"provider\": null,\n    \"function_name\": null,\n    \"comm_inputs\": null,\n    \"command\": \"reg query \\\"HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Image File Execution Options\\\\{{entities.application_exe}}\\\"\",\n    \"fallback_command\": null,\n    \"fallback_sop_id\": null,\n    \"parse_instruction\": null,\n    \"execute_if\": \"variables.ifeo_removed == 'true'\",\n    \"timeout_seconds\": 30\n  }\n]\n\n## MANDATORY CoT INSPECTION CHECKS:\nBefore outputting the final verdict, complete these 3 inspection reasoning checks in order:\n\n- **Check 1 (100% Action & Tool Recall & Preservation)**: Verify that EVERY SINGLE automated procedure step described in the raw human text (whether a shell CLI command like `ipconfig`/`chkdsk` OR an API tool action like `unlock_user_account`/`admin_reset_password`) is preserved in the OKF steps. If any automated action or tool call is missing from the OKF steps, you MUST mark `is_faithful = false` and add it to `dropped_commands`.\n  *(HUMAN CONFIRMATION EXEMPTION: Human/verbal/ticket confirmations, user clarifications, and manual admin approval steps are currently PAUSED. DO NOT flag omitted verbal/ticket/user confirmation steps as dropped commands.)*\n  *(GUI SETUP EXEMPTION: GUI setup steps such as \"Open Command Prompt\", \"Press Windows Key\", \"Run as administrator\", \"Open Web Browser\", or opening UI windows are intentionally omitted from executable playbooks. DO NOT flag GUI setup steps or UI window launches as dropped commands.)*\n  *(TOOL PARAMETER MAPPING EXEMPTION: When an automated search or query step maps to a registered API tool whose interface requires a specific input key (such as `search_users` requiring `email`), passing the query entity like `{entities.email}` or `{entities.partial_detail}` in `comm_inputs` satisfies the step. Do NOT flag other raw search criteria like name or empl